<section class="panel" aria-label="Grade 3 Unit 4 Lesson 4 Interpret Division Expressions">
<h2>Number Talk — subtract mentally</h2><p>500 − 475 = 25; 504 − 475 = 29; 512 − 475 = 37; 512 − 449 = 63. Explain how raising the first number or lowering the second changes the difference.</p>
<h2>Spinning Tops — source order, mathematical matches</h2><table class="source-chart"><thead><tr><th>Situation</th><th>Division expression</th><th>Quotient</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Clare, four equally represented colours</td><td>C: 24 ÷ 4</td><td>6 per colour</td></tr><tr><td>Priya, two painters</td><td>A: 24 ÷ 2</td><td>12 each</td></tr><tr><td>Shop, six boxes</td><td>E: 24 ÷ 6</td><td>4 per box</td></tr><tr><td>Diego, two per friend</td><td>B: 12 ÷ 2</td><td>6 friends</td></tr><tr><td>Six friends, twelve dreidels</td><td>D: 12 ÷ 6</td><td>2 each</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The 2021 original uses photos of culturally varied tops; Edulytics does not reproduce those third-party photographs.</p>
<h2>Cars in Boxes — one expression, two questions</h2><p>21 ÷ 3 = 7. If Han has <strong>three boxes</strong>, each box contains <strong>seven cars</strong>. If Han puts <strong>three cars in each box</strong>, he needs <strong>seven boxes</strong>. The divisor describes different known quantities.</p>
